course: dictionary
lesson: 11643
title: Arrogance: thinking you are better
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Arrogance is a noun. It means behaving as if you are more important, cleverer or better than other people. «The king was full of arrogance and would not listen to his advisers.» Full of arrogance means the king was very proud and acted as if he knew best.
explain: Arrogance can also mean too much pride that makes someone rude or unwilling to listen. «Her arrogance made the other players feel small.» Ask yourself: does this person think they are better than everyone, or refuse to hear other ideas? If yes, arrogance is the word you need.
explain: The opposite of arrogance is humility, which means being modest and willing to learn from others. In many stories, a character who shows arrogance learns a lesson, often the hard way.
fact: Arrogance means behaving as if you are more important, cleverer or better than other people.
fact: Arrogance is uncountable, so we say «arrogance», never «an arrogance» or «arrogances».
fact: Useful phrases: full of arrogance, the arrogance of, sheer arrogance.
fact: In ethics and religious lessons, arrogance is seen as a fault, the opposite of humility.
fact: «The arrogance of the fox made him think he was too clever to be caught.»
exercise: «The boy showed arrogance when he laughed at the team that lost.» What is arrogance here? | Feeling tired after the game | *Acting as if he was better than the others | Running very fast | Being kind and helping them up
exercise: «She walked in, full of arrogance.» What does full of arrogance mean? | Ready to go to sleep | *Very proud and sure she was better than others | Covered in paint from head to toe | Very hungry
exercise: In stories, what often happens to a character who shows arrogance? | They are rewarded straight away | They turn into animals | They forget how to read | *They often learn a lesson
test: «Humility is the opposite of arrogance.» What is humility? | *Being modest and willing to learn from others | Being loud in class | Being happy all the time | Thinking you are the cleverest
test: Which word fits best? «The ___ of the captain made him ignore the storm warnings.» | *arrogance | humility | hunger | sadness
exam: What does «sheer arrogance» most likely mean? | Being very tired after school | *Complete, total pride that ignores other people | A light, gentle breeze | Sharing a snack with a friend
